Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 04:15:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Shopify product-level sales reporting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AUDIT_REPORT.md flagged this as missing (High). fetchShopifyProductFacts
(shopify.ts) does its own paginated pass over orders.json with line_items
in the field list, aggregating sales/quantity/order-count per product —
Shopify's REST Admin API has no dedicated top-products report endpoint on
non-Plus plans, so this derives it the way most third-party apps do,
mirroring the existing fetchShopifyDailyFacts pagination shape rather
than touching that function's working contract.

getLiveShopifyProducts (new shopify-products-live.ts) wraps it with the
same cache/multi-connection/partial-failure pattern as every other live
report, reusing shopify-live.ts's now-exported resolveCreds/cached/
reasonFor. Deliberately NOT merged across connections the way daily
totals are: Shopify product ids are only unique within one store, so
summing across two different connected stores risked silently combining
two unrelated products that happen to share a numeric id.

Wired into the Shopify report as a new "Top products" table (top 50 by
sales), shown on both the internal dashboard and client portal Shopify
pages, live-mode only — no demo-data equivalent, same as the ads
channels' deeper breakdowns.

